    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment (format `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) on owner creation. Since DTOs are OpenAPI-generated and the test DB (hsqldb) uses `ddl-auto=none` with SQL-file schemas, the change spanned several layers:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter, so the value is stored and read back on `GET`.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, assign the code before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (`Math.min(3, len)` guards short names).\n   - `NNNN` = `String.format(\"%04d\", findAllOwners().size() + 1)` \u2014 a global sequence equal to one more than the current owner count. Because each create is saved (and Hibernate auto-flushes before the next query), the count increments across creates, so the second owner's number is exactly one more than the first's \u2014 satisfying the test's `SMI-...`/`JON-...` sequence assertion.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and it's serialized in responses. MapStruct maps it automatically by name (`Owner.getCustomerCode` \u2192 `OwnerDto`).\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"customerCode\", ignore = true)` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (the code is server-assigned, not client-supplied).\n\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to each `owners` table (nullable, so existing seed rows are unaffected).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` verifies both the `LAST3-` prefix format and the global sequence increment, and it passes.",
